              "response": "The mass media reinforce stereotypes mainly by being the only teacher most Canadians ever get. Film invented the pictures: Hollywood's historically inaccurate westerns put made-up, makeup-wearing “bad guys” on screen for suspense, shaping the mainstream image for generations (Sources D–E, p. 168). Television priced them: heavy coverage portrays costly problems and threatened violence while organising almost nothing from an Aboriginal perspective (Source H, p. 168). That is the chapter's thesis in action — media reinforcing the attitudes they find rather than challenging them — though the same screens can dispel stereotypes when makers turn them around (Source B, p. 167).",
