              "extract": "Indigenous peoples share histories that include cultural suppression, economic hardship, discrimination, and racism. They now face common issues as a result of their histories. Some of the challenges faced by indigenous peoples have a geopolitical aspect: a combination of geographic and political factors that relate to or influence a nation or region. For example, in many areas, national borders drawn across ancestral lands have physically divided populations of indigenous peoples. The Blackfoot and Mohawk nations now exist on both sides of the United States–Canada border. Inuit people live in four countries: Canada, Greenland, Russia, and the United States."
